'''Aristotle'''
#an ancient [[Greek]] [[philosopher]], student of [[Plato]] who was a student of [[Socrates.]] Introduced into [[Christian]][[ theology]] by [[Thomas Aquinas]]; philosophical opposite of Plato. This opposition is a major obstacle in [[Western philosophy]], causing major rifts in all the skills of thinking including art, science, physics, politics, etc. Phil. 101 [[User:Cec|Cec]] 09:34, 19 February 2007 (UTC)

